{"id": "EUVD-2026-15332", "enisaUuid": "c455fb72-6a6d-34fa-a86a-1e80626e2ac0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: mcp251x: fix deadlock in error path of mcp251x_open\n\nThe mcp251x_open() function call free_irq() in its error path with the\nmpc_lock mutex held. But if an interrupt already occurred the\ninterrupt handler will be waiting for the mpc_lock and free_irq() will\ndeadlock waiting for the handler to finish.\n\nThis issue is similar to the one fixed in commit 7dd9c26bd6cf (\"can:\nmcp251x: fix deadlock if an interrupt occurs during mcp251x_open\") but\nfor the error path.\n\nTo solve this issue move the call to free_irq() after the lock is\nreleased. Setting `priv->force_quit = 1` beforehand ensure that the IRQ\nhandler will exit right away once it acquired the lock.", "datePublished": "2026-03-25T10:27:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:14:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/739454057572cb0948658d1142f3fa2c6966465c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/416c18ecddafab0ed09be1e7b9d2f448f3d4db16", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/256f0cff6e946c570392bda1d01a65e789a7afd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b73832292cd914e87a55e863ba4413a907e7db6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38063cc435b69d56e76f947c10d336fcb2953508", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d27f12c3f5e85efc479896af4a69eccb37f75e8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e728f444c913a91d290d1824b4770780bbd6378e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab3f894de216f4a62adc3b57e9191888cbf26885"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23357", "GHSA-f94p-fcww-cpfj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "083eac62-06fd-38a6-b1ce-2be4d2918c5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf66f3736a945dd4e92d86427276c6eeab0a6c1d <416c18ecddafab0ed09be1e7b9d2f448f3d4db16"}, {"id": "15a31111-f8e2-3a5a-8c80-ee8c2a8f310c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_